            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Marianne"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a good, solid salad dressing! I did use olive oil rather than the vegetable oil, and my vinegar was white balsamic--a nice complement to the flavors of herbs. I used my garlic press rather than mincing. I like that the herbs used are what I always have on hand! Thanks for the good measurements!",
            "datePublished": "2012-04-15T16:04:30.710Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "CarolynCooks"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very tasty. I substituted oregano for the marjoram so it could be used for Greek salad. I also added a squeeze of lemon. Will make again. Nice combination of herbs, which could be be doubled for a stronger flavor.",
            "datePublished": "2015-12-23T15:09:09.960Z"
